    {
      "id": "GqPWlwkgOOeQUNe0oFpNZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 321,
      "y": 697,
      "width": 808.8394775390625,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1961211967,
      "version": 639,
      "versionNonce": 1783270815,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793733652964,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Change the url\n    - GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v1/vendors\n            - \n    GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v2/vendors\n   - GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v2/catalog\n\n- Custom Http Header\n    - This one sucks the most, IMO, don't think about it.\n    - There really is no such thing as custom http headers.\n\n- Content Negotiation\n    - You can have the user request the version they want with the Accept header.\n    \n\nGET /vendors\nAccept: application/vnd.company.vendor-2+json\n\n\nGET /employees/{id}\nAccept: image/jpg\n\n\n- There is a fourth way - change the authority.\n\nGET https://api-2.company.com/software-center/vendors\n\n\n\n    \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Change the url\n    - GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v1/vendors\n            - \n    GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v2/vendors\n   - GET https://api.company.com/software-center/v2/catalog\n\n- Custom Http Header\n    - This one sucks the most, IMO, don't think about it.\n    - There really is no such thing as custom http headers.\n\n- Content Negotiation\n    - You can have the user request the version they want with the Accept header.\n    \n\nGET /vendors\nAccept: application/vnd.company.vendor-2+json\n\n\nGET /employees/{id}\nAccept: image/jpg\n\n\n- There is a fourth way - change the authority.\n\nGET https://api-2.company.com/software-center/vendors\n\n\n\n    \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ChVLzyfJCuluZQBk2O9yk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 255,
      "y": 1327,
      "width": 876.579345703125,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 54733375,
      "version": 484,
      "versionNonce": 900826801,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793735004407,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"You must design your API before building it\".\n    - when Swagger/Swashbuckle, etc. came out - nobody was allowed to use them.\n\n\n\nSome ways to make it so you don't break clients:\n\n- \"Quiet quit\" - don't make crap up nobody needs. Build for a specific client when possible.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"You must design your API before building it\".\n    - when Swagger/Swashbuckle, etc. came out - nobody was allowed to use them.\n\n\n\nSome ways to make it so you don't break clients:\n\n- \"Quiet quit\" - don't make crap up nobody needs. Build for a specific client when possible.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
